# runner (K4): ops/Dockerfile.runner, ops/railway.runner.json. Railway project: the OPERATOR's (keys), ONE replica.
# Every variable ops/src/runner.ts parseRunnerConfig, identity.ts, log.ts and the steps read.
#
# KEYS AT A GLANCE (docs/v9/solana-migration.md §5, the Solana home):
#   required  OPERATOR_IDENTITY_PEM (secret), CANISTER_ID
#   required for the Ethereum NFT step (on by default)  OPENSEA_API_KEY (secret): listings, fulfillment data, floor evidence
#   optional  RELAY_API_KEY (secret): Relay's /quote/v2 is keyless today; a key raises the rate limit (v2 retires 2026-11-24, Q5 §8)
#   required  UNISAT_API_KEY (secret) for the frog floor reading (RUNNER_FROG_FLOOR=on, the default): the feed believes a listed outpoint
#             only when two providers agree, and only UniSat and ordinals.com serve outputs (Ordinals Wallet does not): without it every
#             listing is L-unverified and no reading is ever handed in (measured 2026-10-10; /healthz is 503). Also the UniSat buying step's
#   optional  RUNNER_COINGECKO_KEY (secret): CoinGecko's demo key for the frog floor's 20 % band reference (keyless by default)
#   optional  SOL_RPC_URLS: the runner's own reads for rule S3 (Relay's depository not upgraded); without it S3 is the canister's alone
#   optional  ETH_LOGS_RPC (secret when keyed): required only while holder deposits are on (eth_nft.deposits)
# SECRET = set in Railway's UI as a service variable (sealed), never in git, a shell history or a shared variable.
# <...> = a deploy-time value (from deployments/canister-ic.json / the ceremony log).

# --- identity and canister -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRET. `dfx identity export <the runner's identity>` (secp256k1 EC PRIVATE KEY or Ed25519 PKCS#8; escaped \n accepted).
# Read only in ops/src/identity.ts:23. Its principal must be the install argument's `operator`. Unset = the runner refuses to tick.
OPERATOR_IDENTITY_PEM=
# the buyer canister id (runner.ts:45; required, refused if not a canister id)
CANISTER_ID=<buyer canister id>
# default https://icp-api.io (ic.ts IC_HOST); https only
IC_HOST=https://icp-api.io

# --- the home (docs/v9/solana-migration.md §5) -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# solana (default) | robinhood (the EVM-era flow, unchanged). Name it ROOK_HOME: HOME is the Unix home directory (read as a home only
# when it is exactly "solana" or "robinhood"; setting HOME=solana on Railway works but moves node's home directory, so prefer ROOK_HOME).
ROOK_HOME=solana
# OPTIONAL. https Solana RPCs, comma-separated (decision D-h: Helius free + PublicNode / Ankr free), each asked at finalized and required to
# agree. Used for rule S3 only (Relay's depository state and ProgramData). Helius keeps its key in the query: set the WHOLE value sealed
# (log.ts scrubs every URL of it). Unset: S3 is checked by the canister alone (it always is).
SOL_RPC_URLS=https://mainnet.helius-rpc.com/?api-key=<HELIUS_KEY>,https://solana-rpc.publicnode.com
# The frog floor READING (D-i: the canister is the registry keeper and posts it; the runner hands it in with frog_floor_reading(coll, …)).
# Ordinals multi-collection (docs/v9/ordinals-collections.md §4): every LIVE Inscriptions collection of frog_collections() is read, each
# paired with its nft-pilot.json listing by members root, and handed in only inside the 20 % band of CoinGecko's floor (§5 step 2, the
# monitor's D8 band): out of the band, or CoinGecko silent, the reading is held (GET /floors says why) and the module keeps its last post.
# A fresh install starts every Inscriptions listing LIVE (default-live, decision 2026-10-12): no frog_wake at the ceremony; frog_sleep is the brake.
# default on (solana home only). Off: nobody feeds the frog modules' floors (they go stale at 3 h; mint / advance stop).
RUNNER_FROG_FLOOR=on
# default 1800, 300..3600 (the canister drops a reading not posted within the hour; rook_core's FLOOR_TTL is 3 h)
RUNNER_FROG_FLOOR_EVERY_S=1800
# canister (default): the canister's LIVE Inscriptions collections are read and posted. all: every DORMANT listing not marked wrapping
# "later" is also read and served at GET /floors, marked "held" (never posted: a collection put to sleep with frog_sleep, until frog_wake lifts it), which is how the wake
# check's book side (≥ 3 valid listings within 20 % of CoinGecko) is watched before a wake. "all" costs Ordinals Wallet / ordinals.com /
# UniSat reads per listing per pass.
RUNNER_FLOOR_LISTINGS=canister
# OPTIONAL SECRET. CoinGecko's demo key (x-cg-demo-api-key, sent only to api.coingecko.com; scrubbed from logs): the band gate's reference,
# /nfts/<coingeckoId> per live collection per pass. Keyless works (CoinGecko's public rate limit; one call per collection per 30 min).
# RUNNER_COINGECKO_KEY=
# default on (solana home only): a holder deposit waiting for its membership proof (holder_deposits(): AwaitingProof or Parked) gets
# frog_proof(coll, inscription, proof) from the LIVE collection whose members file holds it (the launch file's membersFile, baked into the
# image, each checked against the canister's root before it is used; a mismatch is a /healthz problem). Once per deposit per 6 h.
RUNNER_FROG_PROOFS=on
# default: the image's /app/deployments/launch/nft-pilot.json (the listings, their Ordinals Wallet slugs, members files and CoinGecko ids)
# RUNNER_LAUNCH_FILE=/app/deployments/launch/nft-pilot.json

# --- Solana NFT floor evidence (docs/v9/solana-nfts-canister.md §5; src/solnftfloor.ts) --------------------------------------
# default on (the Solana home): for every Solana collection the canister has OPEN (a collection opens on its first request), Magic
# Eden's keyless listings (listingAggMode) and stats, handed in with sol_nft_evidence. Off on the EVM home.
RUNNER_SOL_NFT_FLOOR=on
# default 1800, 300..3600: each open collection at most this often; one Magic Eden call at a time, 0.6 s apart
# RUNNER_SOL_NFT_FLOOR_EVERY_S=1800
# default: the image's /app/deployments/launch/solana-collections.json (the collections and their Magic Eden symbols)
# RUNNER_SOL_COLLECTIONS_FILE=/app/deployments/launch/solana-collections.json
# default https://api-mainnet.magiceden.dev (keyless; https only)
# MAGIC_EDEN_API=https://api-mainnet.magiceden.dev

# --- cadence ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# default 600, 60..86400 (runner.ts:50). Each tick costs cycles (docs/deploy/canister-mainnet.md)
RUNNER_TICK_EVERY_S=600
# ROOK_HOME=robinhood ONLY (not read on the Solana home: the pending cadence followed 4663's state window, which Solana does not have).
# LAUNCH VALUE 120 (docs/v7/phase1-nft.md §5.1; review7 task 5, review8). Default 120; digits only, 60..300 and <= RUNNER_TICK_EVERY_S
# (PENDING_EVERY_MAX_S=300: the runner refuses more). A PERIOD from the signing cycle's start while a 4663 tx is out.
# RUNNER_PENDING_EVERY_S=120
# docs/v7/dormant-collections.md §7: the tick while every collection is DORMANT and nothing is open (from RUNNER_TICK_EVERY_S to 3600;
# default 900). A tick then reads only the wake desk: this is the idle burn. A bonded wake request waits at most this for its tick.
RUNNER_IDLE_TICK_EVERY_S=900
# status port: /healthz, /status. The image sets PORT=8080 (Railway injects PORT too); RUNNER_STATUS_PORT is the fallback name (runner.ts:56)
PORT=8080
# RUNNER_STATUS_PORT=

# --- Relay conversion step (frogs, Bitcoin; docs/v6/relay-conversion.md) ---------------------------------------------------
# default on (runner.ts:59); does nothing while no frog conversion asks for a quote. LAUNCH VALUE on: ordinals at launch (nft-pilot.json
# `bitcoin`, the operator 2026-10-09) converts each Bitcoin Frogs advance through Relay (frog_funding max_fee_bps 400), in the same
# tick as the Ethereum step (docs/v8/ordinals-wave.md §3.4); one Relay leg canister-wide across both sides (B-L-6, fixed in aaf44c5)
RUNNER_RELAY=on
# default https://api.relay.link (relay.ts RELAY_API_DEFAULT); https only. The Ethereum NFT step uses the same API. On the Solana home
# the runner asks /quote/v2 (spike Q5), every leg with a Solana side: SOL -> BTC (frog conversions), SOL -> ETH (an Ethereum buy's
# advance), ETH -> SOL (its way back), for exactly the canister's ask (its Relay key the depositor, its main address every refund: A5-03).
RELAY_API_URL=https://api.relay.link
# OPTIONAL SECRET. Sent as x-api-key to RELAY_API_URL only (read at each call; scrubbed from logs). Keyless works today.
RELAY_API_KEY=

# --- Ethereum NFT step (docs/v7/phase1-nft.md §6) ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# default on (runner.ts:63); does nothing while eth_nft_config() is null
RUNNER_ETH_NFT=on
# 0x<collection>=<opensea slug>,... (ethnft.ts:379 parseSlugs: address 0x+40 hex, slug [a-z0-9-]+). The eleven allowlisted collections (Identity MD since 2026-10-09) of
# deployments/launch/nft-pilot.json (openseaSlug), in its order (docs/v7/dormant-collections.md §1: a dormant one gets no evidence). Every collection the canister serves must be named (ethnft.ts:374).
ETH_NFT_SLUGS=0x5af0d9827e0c53e4799bb226655a1de152a425a5=milady,0xed5af388653567af2f388e6224dc7c4b3241c544=azuki,0x60e4d786628fea6478f785a6d7e704777c86a7c6=mutant-ape-yacht-club,0xbd3531da5cf5857e7cfaa92426877b022e612cf8=pudgypenguins,0xbc4ca0eda7647a8ab7c2061c2e118a18a936f13d=boredapeyachtclub,0x8a90cab2b38dba80c64b7734e58ee1db38b8992e=doodles-official,0x23581767a106ae21c074b2276d25e5c3e136a68b=moonbirds,0x49cf6f5d44e70224e2e23fdcdd2c053f30ada28b=clonex,0x524cab2ec69124574082676e6f654a18df49a048=lilpudgys,0x036721e5a769cc48b3189efbb9cce4471e8a48b1=vv-checks-originals,0x0000ec93127baa929e58e97dd0095a2bfb38ec1d=identitymd
# SECRET. OpenSea API key: listings + fulfillment data (keyed). Read at each call (runner.ts:213,220), scrubbed from logs (log.ts:21).
OPENSEA_API_KEY=
# SECRET when keyed. An https Ethereum RPC serving eth_getLogs (runner.ts:67): recent sales / floor evidence and, with deposits on (D5),
# every NFT sent to the canister's Ethereum address in the last day (DEPOSIT_LOOKBACK_BLOCKS 7,200, in ETH_LOGS_MAX_BLOCKS chunks).
# Without it: no deposit is ever discovered (ethnft.ts:372). Launch: the operator's Dwellir URL (the decision of 2026-09-27), the key in
# the path: https://api-ethereum-mainnet.n.dwellir.com/<DWELLIR_API_KEY>. Set the WHOLE URL as a sealed variable (the runner does not
# expand ${...}; a Railway reference such as https://api-ethereum-mainnet.n.dwellir.com/${{shared.DWELLIR_API_KEY}} also works).
# Errors print only its host (ethnft.ts:207). Keyless fallback (measured 2026-09-27, 500-block ranges at any depth, but an anonymous rate
# limit): https://xrpc.cl/eth. NEVER put this keyed URL into the canister's install argument.
ETH_LOGS_RPC=
# default 500 (runner.ts:69; Dwellir's plan: 500 blocks per eth_getLogs), 10..10,000
ETH_LOGS_MAX_BLOCKS=500
# Robinhood Chain NFTs (2026-10-12, robinhood-everything.md §3): a collection of chain 4663 (EthCollection.chain_id) is served from the
# canister's 4663 side (eth_nft_state_of(4663), read every pass beside eth_nft_state()); its OpenSea slug goes in ETH_NFT_SLUGS like any
# other, and OpenSea is asked under this chain name. Default "robinhood": NOT verified against OpenSea's chain list (read it there, with
# the key, before the first 4663 collection is pinned, and set it here if it differs).
# OPENSEA_CHAIN_4663=robinhood

# --- not read by the runner (listed so they are not set here by mistake) -----------------------------------------------------
# ALERT_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=   (only scrubbed from log lines if present, ops/src/log.ts:19; the runner sends no alert: leave unset here)
# NODE_ENV=production is set by the image. No volume: the canister keeps the state.

# --- Inscriptions buying, per collection (docs/v8/ow-protected.md §4; ops/src/inscriptions.ts) -------------------------------------
# OFF unless set. Ordinals multi-collection: <slug>=<owSlug>:<membersFile>[:<unisat>],… one entry per collection whose listings the
# runner buys: Ordinals Wallet's PROTECTED listings under owSlug (empty: off), then, in a cycle where that handed nothing in, UniSat's
# fixed-price listings under <unisat> (needs UNISAT_API_KEY), each inscription proved from membersFile. The canister's collection is the
# one whose root is the file's tree root (frog_collections()); a collection is served only while live (frog_wake); one Bitcoin hand-in per
# cycle across every collection (the float is shared), the collections in turn. The members files of every nft-pilot.json listing are
# in the image (/app/deployments/launch/btc/<slug>-members.json). E.g., once each has passed its rehearsal:
# RUNNER_INSCRIPTIONS=bitcoin-frogs=bitcoin-frogs:/app/deployments/launch/btc/bitcoin-frogs-members.json:bitcoin-frogs,nodemonkes=nodemonkes:/app/deployments/launch/btc/nodemonkes-members.json
#
# The one-collection form below still reads, as Bitcoin Frogs' entry (bitcoin-frogs=<RUNNER_OW_SLUG>:<RUNNER_OW_MEMBERS>[:<RUNNER_UNISAT_COLLECTION>]);
# refused beside a RUNNER_INSCRIPTIONS that names bitcoin-frogs too.
# Ordinals Wallet protected listings: the Bitcoin collection's Ordinals Wallet slug (e.g. bitcoin-frogs). The canister must have the
# protected-buy build (frog_offer_protected), reviewed, and one funded rehearsal must have passed before this is turned on.
# LAUNCH VALUE bitcoin-frogs (deployments/launch/btc/README.md; nft-pilot.json bitcoin.owSlug), once the protected-buy build is reviewed
# and installed AND one funded rehearsal has passed (the operator declined it for now: docs/v7/golive-runbook.md §9, open items). Until
# then Bitcoin buys are the operator's manual hand-ins (`npm run offer`, ordinals-wave §3.4)
# RUNNER_OW_SLUG=bitcoin-frogs
# Required with RUNNER_OW_SLUG: a JSON array of the collection's inscription ids, the leaves of the listing's membership root, in the
# deploy's order (a file in the image or on a volume)
# LAUNCH VALUE the file baked into the runner image
# RUNNER_OW_MEMBERS=/app/deployments/launch/btc/bitcoin-frogs-members.json

# --- UniSat fixed-price listings (ops/src/unisatbuy.ts) --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OFF unless set: the Bitcoin collection's UniSat collection id. Its listings go to the canister's CLASSIC judge (frog_offer), which
# refuses any PSBT whose seller input is not already signed: the shape of UniSat's create_bid answer is verified only by a funded buy.
# Tried only in a cycle where the protected step handed nothing in. Uses RUNNER_OW_MEMBERS for membership. One bid per frog per 30 min.
# LAUNCH VALUE bitcoin-frogs (after one funded rehearsal)
# RUNNER_UNISAT_COLLECTION=bitcoin-frogs
# SECRET. UniSat's open-api key (sent only to open-api.unisat.io; scrubbed from logs). REQUIRED on the Solana home for the frog floor
# reading (keeper/src/ordapi.ts mainnetFeed: UniSat + ordinals.com are the two output readers that must agree), and with
# RUNNER_UNISAT_COLLECTION or a RUNNER_INSCRIPTIONS entry with a UniSat id.
UNISAT_API_KEY=
